' --- Diagram: Path A (HTTP) vs Path B (PowerShell) comparison ---
@startuml
title Dynamic analysis paths — comparison A vs B
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

left to right direction

package "Path A — VM Agent HTTP" #E3F2FD {
  [Frontend / API] as A_FE
  [VM Orchestrator\nvm_orchestrator.py] as A_VMO
  [hyperv or proxmox\ndriver] as A_DRV
  [Hyper-V VM] as A_VM
  [vm-agent\nMinimal API] as A_AGENT
}

package "Path B — PowerShell Hyper-V" #FFF9C4 {
  [WPF Desktop] as B_WPF
  [04-Run-Sample.ps1\n+ RunSample phases] as B_PS
  [Hyper-V VM] as B_VM
  [Run-MalwareAnalysis.ps1\n+ Sysmon] as B_GUEST
}

' *Path A: backend orchestrator via HTTP*
A_FE --> A_VMO : POST /api/analysis
A_VMO --> A_DRV
A_DRV --> A_VM : restore snapshot\nstart / stop
A_DRV --> A_AGENT : HTTP REST\nupload · run · report
A_AGENT --> A_VM

' *Path B: local WPF orchestration + PsDirect*
B_WPF --> B_PS : local orchestration
B_PS --> B_VM : restore snapshot\nCopy-VMFile / PsDirect
B_PS --> B_GUEST : guest credentials
B_GUEST --> B_VM

note bottom of A_AGENT
  Basic telemetry
  (process, stdout/stderr)
  Orchestrator: backend
end note

note bottom of B_GUEST
  Full telemetry
  (files, registry, network)
  Orchestrator: WPF / scripts
end note

note as N1
  **Independent** — HTTP vs PsDirect.
  Both use Internal switch and CleanState snapshot.
  The hyperv driver **does not** invoke 04-Run-Sample.ps1.
end note

@enduml
